{"id": "EUVD-2026-82110", "enisaUuid": "caceba05-8fed-3fa3-90b4-b789ef8a3a8e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: Fix skb double-free in xfrm_dev_direct_output()\n\nA return value other than 1 from local_out() means that the skb has been\nconsumed or its ownership was transferred. xfrm_dev_direct_output()\nnevertheless frees the skb on this path, causing a double-free when\nnetfilter drops the packet and invalidating any other owner.\n\nReturn the local_out() result directly, matching the ownership handling\nin xfrm_output_resume().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:55", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/621871b696b108026bf4b44ed4085ffa2102f417", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc9297796bfdcc8d9609236e54519a4f38737aac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02deb637e965950148752a304dd1471212dd6470", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56a347950e661c1a7f8f31c43a2ea53c2323b6f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2aed51fc58d9ce450e2c116efb956160fd06fa02"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92489", "GHSA-x3mf-vgc4-phvg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0016ac68-d42d-338b-88fa-6878d2d75aba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a0395e96831adee8ffa016bf958e4dce9ece656e <bc9297796bfdcc8d9609236e54519a4f38737aac"}, {"id": "0fc5047f-7f26-38f7-88f6-b91224b1cbcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13.9 <6.14"}, {"id": "29ca3bde-7f7d-37f9-b0d6-7173bbff57fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2e46e192-c6e7-3a04-8563-169a195877af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.85 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "35d85509-58ce-3665-8da6-5c8fbf5f750a", "product": {"name": "